$ factory serve -h
exit 0
--- stdout
usage: factory serve [flags]

Serve the HTTP API until interrupted, then shut down gracefully.
Refuses to start against a database that is behind this binary's migrations.
The --launcher flags start worker sandboxes as Kubernetes Jobs and need
in-cluster config.

Flags (each also read from FACTORY_<FLAG>, e.g. FACTORY_ADDR):
  --addr ADDRESS
      listen address (default 127.0.0.1:8080)
  --database-url URL
      Postgres URL
  --github-api-url URL
      GitHub REST API base URL (default https://api.github.com)
  --github-app-id ID
      GitHub App ID that mints workers' repository tokens; set it with
      --github-app-key-file, or leave both unset
  --github-app-key-file FILE
      the GitHub App's PEM private key file
  --launcher
      run the launcher and the server-side steps
  --launcher-allowed-images STRING
      comma-separated image repository prefixes, such as
      ghcr.io/autobutler-org/, a repository's image (image in
      .factory/config.toml) may come from; a prefix without a trailing / is
      one repository. Empty lets no repository choose its image
  --launcher-api-token-secret NAME
      Secret name in the worker namespace whose key "token" is given to
      workers as FACTORY_API_TOKEN (default factory-worker-api-token)
  --launcher-capabilities STRING
      comma-separated capabilities the worker image registers; items requiring
      others are left alone (default claude-code)
  --launcher-image IMAGE
      worker image; required with --launcher
  --launcher-limits STRING
      cpu, memory and ephemeral-storage limits of the worker container
      (default cpu=4,memory=8Gi,ephemeral-storage=20Gi)
  --launcher-max-sandboxes INT
      most worker sandboxes alive at once (default 4)
  --launcher-model-key-secret NAME
      Secret name in the worker namespace whose key "api-key" is given to
      workers as ANTHROPIC_API_KEY (default factory-model-api-key)
  --launcher-namespace NAMESPACE
      namespace the worker Jobs run in (default factory-workers)
  --launcher-node-selector STRING
      key=value,... node selector for worker pods
  --launcher-pending-timeout DURATION
      destroy a sandbox still pending after this long (an image that will not
      pull, a pod that cannot be scheduled) and start a new one; 0 never does
      (default 10m0s)
  --launcher-requests STRING
      cpu, memory and ephemeral-storage requests of the worker container
      (default cpu=1,memory=2Gi,ephemeral-storage=10Gi)
  --launcher-runtime-class NAME
      RuntimeClass name of worker pods, such as gvisor
  --launcher-server-url URL
      URL workers reach this server at; required with --launcher
  --launcher-service-account NAME
      ServiceAccount name of worker pods (default factory-worker)
  --launcher-tolerations STRING
      key=value:Effect or key:Effect,... tolerations for worker pods
  --lease DURATION
      how long a claim lasts without a heartbeat; a worker silent this long is
      marked gone (default 5m0s)
  --max-attempts INT
      failed attempts before a step or item is failed (default 3)
  --retry-delay DURATION
      wait before handing out a retried step or item (default 1m0s)
  --stuck-after DURATION
      revoke a claim with no stage report for this long and count an attempt
      (default 3h0m0s)

Environment:
  FACTORY_API_TOKEN    bearer token required on /api/v1. When unset the API is
                       unauthenticated and --addr must be a loopback address.
--- stderr
